Builds one live CFixedWindow from a declared child-window name. This is what fills the parent window's subwindow map at +0x414, and it is the link that makes the `windowType` keyword and that container one fact.

  - looks `name` up in the gui-type tree embedded at CWindowType +0x150 (slot 1 on the embedded object);
  - if absent, asks `[this+0x14C]` (the CGui) for a default through slot 18, passing the type's own `parent` string at +0x68, and re-looks-up under that name;
  - calls the window factory 0xAC4FE0 with the resolved CWindowType in ESI, which does `operator new(0x4C8)` and CFixedWindow::CFixedWindow - so **a subwindow is a full CFixedWindow**;
  - adjusts the result to its CGuiObject with `lea ebx, [esi + 0x18]` and registers it with the CGui through slot 16;
  - returns the **complete** window pointer.

`ret 0x24`: the name is an Hoi3CString **by value** (0x1C bytes at [ebp+8]..[ebp+0x20]) plus two dwords at [ebp+0x24] and [ebp+0x28], which the factory passes straight through. Receiver in ecx. Two callers: 0xAC0C73, the constructor's subwindow build loop, and 0xAC3C27.
